  "notes": "{矛盾|むじゅん} comes from a Chinese story about a man selling both a spear (⟦{矛|ほこ}→矛：noentry⟧) and a shield (⟦{盾|たて}→盾：03430_tate⟧), claiming each was invincible.\n\nETYMOLOGY: A merchant claimed his spear could pierce any shield, and his shield could block any spear. Someone asked what would happen if his spear struck his shield - exposing the contradiction.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {矛盾|むじゅん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to contradict, be inconsistent\n- {矛盾|むじゅん}⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: to be contradictory\n- {矛盾|むじゅん}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{感|かん}じる→感じる：02044_kanjiru⟧: to feel a contradiction",
